\h Matthew
\toc1 Matthew
\mt1 Matthew
\c 5
\s1 The Sermon on the Mount
\p
\v 1 Seeing the crowds, he went up on the mountain, and when he sat down, his disciples came to him.
\s1 The Beatitudes
\p
\v 2 And he opened his mouth and taught them, saying:
\p
\v 3 \wj “Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.\wj*
\p
\v 4 \wj “Blessed are those who mourn, for they shall be comforted.\wj*
\p
\v 5 \wj “Blessed are the meek, for they shall inherit the earth.\wj*
\p
\v 6 \wj “Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness, for they shall be satisfied.\wj*
\p
\v 7 \wj “Blessed are the merciful, for they shall receive mercy.\wj*
\p
\v 8 \wj “Blessed are the pure in heart, for they shall see God.\wj*
\p
\v 9 \wj “Blessed are the peacemakers, for they shall be called sons\f + \ft Greek huioi; see Preface\f* of God.\wj*
\p
\v 10 \wj “Blessed are those who are persecuted for righteousness' sake, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.\wj*
\p
\v 11 \wj “Blessed are you when others revile you and persecute you and utter all kinds of evil against you falsely on my account.\wj*
\v 12 \wj Rejoice and be glad, for your reward is great in heaven, for so they persecuted the prophets who were before you.\wj*
